BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:heraklion-agios-myronas-panigiri-of-agios-myron-agios-myronas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270809
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Myron\, Agios Myronas
LOCATION:Agios Myronas\, Crete (Heraklion)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:One of the largest panigiria in Crete: the Malevizi village where the saint lived holds a hierarchical vespers and an all-night liturgy on 7 August\, the procession of his relics on the 8th\, and two nights of Cretan music in the main square (Kounalis brothers and Kallergis brothers in 2026). Pilgrims queue for the saint's tomb and the holy-water cave under the church. The village is 20 minutes from Heraklion\; parking is on the approach road\, so come early.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#agios-myronas-panigiri-of-agios-myron-agios-myronas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#agios-myronas-panigiri-of-agios-myron-agios-myronas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
